„­bible_version£KJV¤book§chapter¨sections•…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses–„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙThen came David to Nob to Ahimelech the priest: and Ahimelech was afraid at the meeting of David, and said unto him, Why art thou alone, and no man with thee?¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÚAnd David said unto Ahimelech the priest, The king hath commanded me a business, and hath said unto me, Let no man know any thing of the business whereabout I send thee, and what I have commanded thee: and I have appointed my servants to such and such a place.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙlNow therefore what is under thine hand? give me five loaves of bread in mine hand, or what there is present.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙªAnd the priest answered David, and said, There is no common bread under mine hand, but there is hallowed bread; if the young men have kept themselves at least from women.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÚ
And David answered the priest, and said unto him, Of a truth women have been kept from us about these three days, since I came out, and the vessels of the young men are holy, and the bread is in a manner common, yea, though it were sanctified this day in the vessel.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¯So the priest gave him hallowed bread: for there was no bread there but the shewbread, that was taken from before the LORD, to put hot bread in the day when it was taken away.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses‘„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ­Now a certain man of the servants of Saul was there that day, detained before the LORD; and his name was Doeg, an Edomite, the chiefest of the herdmen that belonged to Saul.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse	¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ½And David said unto Ahimelech, And is there not here under thine hand spear or sword? for I have neither brought my sword nor my weapons with me, because the king's business required haste.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse	¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÚAnd the priest said, The sword of Goliath the Philistine, whom thou slewest in the valley of Elah, behold, it is here wrapped in a cloth behind the ephod: if thou wilt take that, take it: for there is no other save that here. And David said, There is none like that; give it me.¦layout ªlast_verse	…¤book§chapter«first_verse
