¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙYAnd David arose, and fled that day for fear of Saul, and went to Achish the king of Gath.¦layout ªlast_verse
„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines“‚¤textÙŒAnd the servants of Achish said unto him, Is not this David the king of the land? did they not sing one to another of him in dances, saying,¦layout ‚¤text¾Saul hath slain his thousands,¦layout§quote_1‚¤text¼And David his ten thousands?¦layout§quote_1ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ[And David laid up these words in his heart, and was sore afraid of Achish the king of Gath.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses“„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ§And he changed his behaviour before them, and feigned himself mad in their hands, and scrabbled on the doors of the gate, and let his spittle fall down upon his beard.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙhThen said Achish unto his servants, Lo, ye see the man is mad: wherefore then have ye brought him to me?¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ‚Have I need of mad men, that ye have brought this fellow to play the mad man in my presence? shall this fellow come into my house?¦layout ªlast_verse